# License: Free for Non-Commercial Use / Paid Commercial License Required

This project is **source-available**, not permissively "open source" in the
OSI sense. It uses a dual-license structure modeled on common patterns like
the Business Source License and PolyForm Noncommercial.

## 1. Non-Commercial License (Free, No Royalty)

Permission is granted, free of charge, for personal, educational, academic
research and internal non-commercial evaluation use of this software and
associated documentation (the "Software"), including the rights to use,
copy, modify and merge the Software, subject to:

- This license notice and DISCLAIMER.md must be included in all copies or
  substantial portions of the Software.
- The Software may NOT be used to generate revenue, embedded in a
  commercial product or paid service, used within a for-profit
  organization's production systems or resold/relicensed, without a
  Commercial License (Section 2).

## 2. Commercial License (royalty required)

Any use of the Software by, or on behalf of, a for-profit entity in a
production, revenue-generating, client-facing or internally cost-saving
business capacity requires a separate **Commercial License Agreement**
with the copyright holder, Dheeraj Krishna Kumar, including a royalty payable
to the copyright holder. Indicative structure (final terms negotiated per
licensee):

| Term | Default structure |
|---|---|
| Royalty basis | Percentage of net revenue attributable to the licensed product OR flat annual fee |
| Suggested royalty rate | 3-8% of attributable net revenue (negotiable) |
| Reporting | Licensee provides quarterly usage/revenue reports |
| Term | Annual, renewable, with audit rights for the licensor |
| Scope | Defined per licensee (internal use, redistribution, white-label, etc.) |

To request a Commercial License, see [CONTACT.md](CONTACT.md). Until a
signed Commercial License Agreement is in place, no commercial rights are
granted and unauthorized commercial use constitutes copyright infringement
and breach of this license.

## 3. No warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR
OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE.

## 4. Important legal note

This is a template, not a lawyer-drafted, jurisdiction-specific contract. 
Royalty terms are only enforceable via a signed agreement with each
commercial licensee. For real revenue-bearing licensing, have a lawyer
review this before enforcing it and consider registering your copyright.

